SECTION 2. USERS AND ROLES
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Five access levels:
1. Public (no sign-in): residents and visitors. Read-only help information.
2. Viewer: observers or senior officials. Can see the live map, queue and dashboard. Cannot change anything.
3. Field Officer (includes clearance squad members): reports hazards, sees own reports and assignments, updates progress on assigned hazards.
4. Command Officer: verifies reports, dispatches crews, changes status, overrides priority (with a reason), manages alerts, relief camp status and hero-story approvals, exports data.
5. Admin: everything above plus users, crews, zones, help points, page content, activity log and data reset.

