Severity scale from the priority score: 9.0 and above = Critical (red), 7.0 to 8.9 = High (orange #EF6C00), 4.0 to 6.9 = Medium (amber), below 4.0 = Low (green). Severity is ALWAYS shown as colour + word + icon, never colour alone.

Typography: Plus Jakarta Sans (or Inter) for English, Noto Sans Telugu for Telugu, Noto Sans Devanagari for Hindi, with system sans-serif fallbacks. Body text at least 16px. Hero headline 52px bold on desktop and 34px on mobile. Section titles 28px bold. Card titles 20px semibold. Large numbers (stats and priority scores) 36 to 44px extra-bold. Line-height 1.5 for body and 1.2 for headings.

Shape and effects: 12 to 16px rounded corners on cards, 12px on buttons, fully rounded chips, 1px borders, soft shadows that lift slightly on hover. One icon family only (Lucide, 24px, 2px stroke), shown in soft tinted circles for feature tiles. No heavy gradients, no glassmorphism, no neon, no decorative patterns, no oversized decorative icons, no cartoon graphics.

Imagery: the hero uses a realistic documentary-style photograph (licensed or a clearly marked placeholder) of a municipal clearance crew in reflective jackets removing a fallen tree from a wet coastal road after a storm, with palm trees, hills and an emergency vehicle in the background. A soft white-to-transparent fade on the left keeps text readable. All images need alt text. No photos of real identifiable people in the hero or in Our Heroes.

Maps: real street-map appearance using MapLibre GL JS with OpenStreetMap raster or vector tiles, centred on Visakhapatnam (about 17.6868 N, 83.2185 E, zoom 11 to 12), with roads, labels, coast and terrain visible. If the tiles cannot load (offline), automatically switch to a clean local schematic map of Visakhapatnam showing the coast, main roads, hospital routes and zones, and show a small label "Offline map". Never show an empty grey map.

Motion (small and purposeful): numbers count up on first load; critical pins pulse softly; cards lift 4px on hover; drawers and bottom sheets slide in; toasts fade in and out; the ticker scrolls slowly. No parallax, bouncing or spinning effects. If the user prefers reduced motion, turn all of this off and make the ticker static.

